<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Cooked Finance"
  description="How Cooked Finance handles calculator inputs, optional local saving, consent-based analytics, hosting logs, and advertising."
  path="/privacy"
  eyebrow="Privacy"
  heading="Your financial inputs stay in your browser."
  lead="The calculator does not send your age, income, expenses, savings, debt payments, retirement balance, monthly savings, or score to Cooked Finance or Google Analytics."
  updated="August 17, 2026"
>
  <h2>Scope</h2>
  <p>
    This policy explains how Cooked Finance (“we,” “us,” or “our”) handles
    information when you use <strong>cookedfinance.com</strong> (the “Site”).
    The Site is designed to work without an account, bank connection, or
    database profile.
  </p>

  <h2>Calculator information</h2>
  <p>
    The seven values entered into the financial health check and the values
    entered into the standalone calculators are processed locally by code in
    your web browser. They are not submitted to our servers, placed in page
    URLs, or included in analytics events.
  </p>
  <p>
    A result is <strong>not saved automatically</strong>. If you select “Save
    This Check,” the seven inputs, result,
    and save time are stored in your browser’s <code>localStorage</code>. That
    copy remains on that browser and device until you delete it in the result
    controls or clear browser storage.
  </p>

  <h2>Browser storage and retention</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      A saved financial check remains in <code>localStorage</code> until you
      delete it from the homepage controls or clear this site’s browser storage.
    </li>
    <li>
      Your analytics choice remains in <code>localStorage</code> until you change
      it through “Privacy choices” or clear this site’s browser storage.
    </li>
    <li>
      Browser privacy settings, private-browsing behavior, or automatic storage
      cleanup may remove either local item sooner. Cooked Finance cannot restore
      a locally deleted check.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Optional analytics</h2>
  <p>
    Google Analytics loads only after you select “Allow Analytics.” If allowed,
    it may process information such as the page visited, referring page,
    browser and device information, approximate location, and online
    identifiers. We use generic interaction event names to understand whether
    the assessment is useful; we do not attach financial inputs, exact results,
    or score bands to those events.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your analytics choice is stored in <code>localStorage</code>. Choose
    “Privacy choices” in the footer to reopen the consent notice. Selecting
    “Essential Only” disables analytics collection immediately and prevents the
    analytics script from loading on future page views in that browser. If the
    script or analytics cookies were already loaded, they may remain in the
    browser until the page is reloaded or those cookies are deleted.
  </p>
  <p>
    After permission is granted, Google Analytics may set first-party cookies
    including <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_&lt;container-id&gt;</code> to
    distinguish users and preserve session state. Google documents a default
    lifetime of up to two years for those cookies, although browser controls can
    shorten it. User-level and event-level analytics data is retained under the
    property’s configured Google Analytics retention setting; aggregated reports
    are not governed by that same setting. See Google’s
    <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/11397207" rel="noopener" target="_blank">GA4 cookie documentation<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>,
    <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/7667196" rel="noopener" target="_blank">data-retention documentation<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>, and
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener" target="_blank">explanation of how Google uses information from partner sites<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting and security logs</h2>
  <p>
    Our hosting and network providers may process routine request data needed
    to deliver and protect the Site, such as IP address, requested URL,
    timestamp, user agent, and security signals. Those requests do not contain
    calculator fields because calculations happen locally.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    Cooked Finance currently displays no paid ads and has not applied for
    Google AdSense. No AdSense script or ad unit is loaded. If advertising is
    introduced later, this policy and the
    <a href="/advertising-policy/">advertising policy</a> will be updated before
    ads are enabled.
  </p>

  <h2>External links</h2>
  <p>
    Educational pages link to external sources. Their privacy practices are
    controlled by their operators, not Cooked Finance.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    The Site is intended for a general adult audience and is not directed to
    children under 13. We do not knowingly ask children to provide personal
    information.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Use the calculators without saving a result.</li>
    <li>Delete a saved check from the homepage result controls or browser storage.</li>
    <li>Choose “Essential Only” or reopen “Privacy choices” in the footer.</li>
    <li>Use browser controls to clear site storage or restrict scripts.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    Material changes will be posted here with a revised date. For a privacy
    question or deletion concern, use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
